question:
What is logged?
```javascript
localStorage.setItem('key', 'value');
const item = localStorage.getItem('key');
console.log(item);
localStorage.removeItem('key');
console.log(localStorage.getItem('key'));
```

What is the difference between localStorage and sessionStorage?
```javascript
localStorage.setItem('a', '1');
sessionStorage.setItem('b', '2');
```

What is logged?
```javascript
const obj = { a: 1, b: 2 };
localStorage.setItem('obj', obj);
const retrieved = localStorage.getItem('obj');
console.log(typeof retrieved);
```

What is the proper way to store and retrieve an object?
```javascript
const obj = { a: 1 };
localStorage.setItem('obj', JSON.stringify(obj));
const retrieved = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('obj'));
console.log(retrieved.a);
```

What happens?
```javascript
localStorage.setItem('key1', 'value1');
localStorage.setItem('key2', 'value2');
console.log(localStorage.length);
localStorage.clear();
console.log(localStorage.length);
```

What is the storage capacity?
```javascript
try {
  let data = 'x'.repeat(10000000);
  localStorage.setItem('large', data);
} catch (e) {
  console.log(e.name);
}
```

What is logged?
```javascript
window.addEventListener('storage', (e) => {
  console.log(e.key, e.newValue);
});
localStorage.setItem('shared', 'data');
```

What is the output?
```javascript
localStorage.setItem('key', 'value1');
localStorage.setItem('key', 'value2');
console.log(localStorage.getItem('key'));
```

How do you iterate localStorage?
```javascript
for (let i = 0; i < localStorage.length; i++) {
  const key = localStorage.key(i);
  const value = localStorage.getItem(key);
  console.log(key, value);
}
```

